  <name>Viaduct</name>
  <summary>Fast, native RSS reader for Linux</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Viaduct is a native Linux RSS reader built in Rust with GTK4, with its own flat design.
      It aims for full feature parity with NetNewsWire, providing a fast and familiar experience.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Local account support</li>
      <li>Inoreader sync support</li>
      <li>Runs on GNOME, Hyprland, and other Wayland desktops</li>
      <li>Blazing fast FTS5 search</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <developer id="org.virinvictus">
    <name>Brandon LaRocque</name>
  </developer>
